{
  "id": "pacs.003.001.08",
  "short": "pacs.003",
  "name": "FIToFICustomerDirectDebit",
  "domain": "pacs",
  "label": "FI to FI Customer Direct Debit",
  "direction": "bank → bank",
  "mtEquivalent": ["MT104"],
  "related": ["pain.008", "pacs.002", "pacs.004", "pacs.007"],
  "summary": "Collects money from a debtor's account on the creditor's instruction — the interbank leg of a direct debit. The mirror image of pacs.008: the party sending the message is the one being paid.",
  "whenUsed": "Sent by the creditor agent to the debtor agent after a creditor initiated a collection with pain.008. Carries the mandate reference that authorises the pull, which is what distinguishes a direct debit from an unauthorised debit.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The direction of the message and the direction of the money are opposite. The creditor agent sends it; the funds flow back the other way. Settlement entries are easy to get backwards here.",
    "Sequence Type (FRST, RCUR, FNAL, OOFF) must be consistent with the mandate's history. SEPA rejects a RCUR where no FRST has ever been collected, and this is one of the most common SDD failures.",
    "Mandate Related Information is where the mandate id and signature date live. Without a valid mandate reference the debtor agent has no basis to debit, and a dispute will be resolved against the creditor."
  ],
